{
  "version": 1,
  "provenance": {
    "card_sprite": "Consumer-indexed sprite and animation tables. Three common spans preserve exact pointer identity and decoded target formats; EU language selectors independently establish additional localized tables. Unused trailing animation pointers are individual neutral scalars, not invented extra array elements.",
    "native_catalog_sections": "The existing card-sprite catalog groups frame lists and animation descriptors for the same runtime resources. Its three common groups form one continuous initialized-data run in US and JP; EU inserts two additional localized sprite groups between them. Ordering only those EU declarations at their existing positions produces one ordinary data section per version. Types, initializers, object bounds and every relocation target are unchanged. The shared catalog TU is retained as a reconstruction model; no original filename or exact asset-generator boundary is claimed."
